title: '2026-11-14: Removing Jeff''s reply from your fork now hides the message it answers. Committed on main as d72791ed.'
pid: e18fd2df-87e7-4bd5-81da-edb58f812e22
body: |2-
  The fault was in what counts as a hide, not in what '⟨node:ID⟩'
  resolves to. All tests pass, with new ones in
  'tests/hidden_from_subscriptions.rs' that fail without the change. A
  fresh reviewer read the change against your words; I took two of its
  points (no unhide on placing; no hide of a member the save still
  holds) and argued against a third, recorded in my note. What I learned is under "what I know", in
  "A child removed from a subscriber hides the subscribee's member it overrides."
